# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in real values.
# Use KEY=value with no spaces around `=`.
#
# NOTE: the Android build does NOT read this file. Build-time configuration
# for the app goes in `local.properties` (gitignored) — see the bottom section.
# `.env` exists only for Taskmaster (the task tool), and even that is optional.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Task Master AI (CLI/MCP) — ALL OPTIONAL with this template.
# .taskmaster/config.json uses the `claude-code` provider, which reuses your
# Claude Code session — no API key needed. Only add keys here if you switch to
# API-based models or want `--research` mode (Perplexity recommended for that).
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-api03-..."
#PERPLEXITY_API_KEY="pplx-..."

# ── Android build configuration — put these in `local.properties`, not here.
#
#   # local.properties (gitignored; created by you, read by Gradle)
#   sdk.dir=/opt/android-sdk
#
#   # Google OAuth Android client id for the Photos Picker API. Not a secret
#   # (Android clients are public clients, there is no client secret), but it
#   # is tied to your package name + signing certificate SHA-1, so keep it
#   # per-developer. Create it at https://console.cloud.google.com/ →
#   # APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth client ID → Android, after enabling
#   # the "Google Photos Picker API" for the project.
#   pomegranate.oauthClientId=1234567890-abc.apps.googleusercontent.com
#
#   # Release signing (optional; the release build stays unsigned without it).
#   # Path is relative to the repo root. See docs/RELEASE.md for creating the key.
#   pomegranate.signing.storeFile=keys/pomegranate-release.jks
#   pomegranate.signing.storePassword=...
#   pomegranate.signing.keyAlias=pomegranate
#   pomegranate.signing.keyPassword=...
#
# Keystores and passwords never go in the repo: `*.jks`/`*.p12` are gitignored
# and local.properties is too.
